        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "#### 4.2. An OOBN Model for GEI at the Italian Province level",
            "block_bbox": [
                96,
                529,
                803,
                557
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    96.0,
                    529.0
                ],
                [
                    803.0,
                    529.0
                ],
                [
                    803.0,
                    557.0
                ],
                [
                    96.0,
                    557.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Figure 6 shows the learned top level of the OOBN for the GEI at the Italian provincial level. Model estimation followed a multi-stage procedure. In the first stage, an exploratory analysis was carried out: a fully data-driven model, initially free from any predefined structure, was estimated to explore associations among extra variables and ingredients. Specifically, the NPC algorithm was employed to investigate these relationships while allowing for certain structural constraints during the learning process. For example, it was assumed that the extra variables held a preliminary position with respect to the gender perspective. Consequently, during the estimation, they were constrained so as not to be influenced by the GEI ingredient variables. This stage enabled the data-driven identification of those extra variables serving as input variables for BN instances. The selection was based on the observed interrelations between extra variables and GEI ingredients that emerged during this exploratory phase, prior to the formal establishment of the GEI architecture via OOBN.",
            "block_bbox": [
                94,
                570,
                996,
                797
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    94.0,
                    570.0
                ],
                [
                    996.0,
                    570.0
                ],
                [
                    996.0,
                    797.0
                ],
                [
                    94.0,
                    797.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In the second stage, each BN instance (one per domain) was learned from data, including both the variables inherently associated with the domain and the extra variables identified as inputs in the previous step (see Section 4.2.1 for details). The model architecture was then finalized by introducing function nodes both for the domains and subdomains within the BN instances and for the overall GEI Indicator.",
            "block_bbox": [
                94,
                799,
                995,
                890
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    94.0,
                    799.0
                ],
                [
                    995.0,
                    799.0
                ],
                [
                    995.0,
                    890.0
                ],
                [
                    94.0,
                    890.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In particular, all BN instances ultimately converge, through the output nodes, to GEI, the OOBN model's target node. GEI is a function node whose values are computed using a weighted geometric mean. To compensate for the unavailable Time domain, the original weights were normalized as follows: 0.22 for Work, 0.18 for Money, 0.26 for Knowledge, 0.12 for Power, and 0.22 for Health. The formula is",
            "block_bbox": [
                95,
                891,
                995,
                982
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    95.0,
                    891.0
                ],
                [
                    995.0,
                    891.0
                ],
                [
                    995.0,
                    982.0
                ],
                [
                    95.0,
                    982.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ GEI=Work Domain^{0.22}*Money Domain^{0.18}*Knowledge Domain^{0.26}*Power Domain^{0.12}*Health Domain^{0.22} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                997,
                976,
                1024
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
